# NOTE: this file currently does NOTHING.
#
# www.alflorna.com is served by GitHub Pages (confirmed: `Server: GitHub.com`),
# and _headers is a Cloudflare Pages / Netlify convention that GitHub Pages
# ignores. Jekyll also skips underscore-prefixed files, which is why
# https://www.alflorna.com/_headers returns 404 rather than the file itself.
#
# Consequence to remember when testing: GitHub Pages serves HTML with
# `Cache-Control: max-age=600` and that is not configurable. A page can be up
# to 10 minutes stale in the browser (and in GitHub's Fastly cache) after a
# push. The ?v= query on styles.css / app.js only helps once the HTML has
# refreshed. Use a private tab if you need to see a change immediately.
#
# Kept here, corrected, so it works if the site ever moves to Cloudflare Pages.

# Was `/*.html`, which never matched anything: Pages serves clean URLs
# (/rsvp, not /rsvp.html), so that rule missed every real page. On /* instead.
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive, noimageindex
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Photos and other assets are fine to cache hard.
/brand_assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/gallery/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
